# Python type annotations

Every project Python function, method, and typed public value must have annotations.

- Annotate all parameters and return types. Use `-> None` for functions that return nothing.
- Annotate module-level constants and locals when the type is not obvious from the right-hand side.
- Do not use bare `Any` to skip typing. Prefer `from __future__ import annotations`.
- Check with `.venv/bin/mypy` before committing. Do not add untyped project scripts.
- This applies to project Python (`scripts/`, and any new project modules). Not vendor code under `.opencode/skills/`.
